<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center"><B>EXPLANATORY NOTE</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">As disclosed earlier, </FONT><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10.5pt">on
February 9, 2026, Ucommune International Ltd (the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;) held an extraordinary general meeting and approved, among
other things, on a date when the closing market price per the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary share is less than US$1.00, or on such
date as any director or chief executive officer of the Company deems advisable and may determine in his or her absolute discretion, a
series of reverse share splits of the Company&rsquo;s authorized share capital. On March 25, 2026, the board of directors of the Company
approved a </FONT><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">reverse share split of all the Company&rsquo;s issued and unissued shares at an exchange
ratio of one (1) share for ten (10) shares (&ldquo;<B>Reverse Share Split</B>&rdquo;). </FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">The Reverse Share Split will be effective at 5:00 P.M. on April 29, 2026
and the Company&rsquo;s Class A Ordinary Shares will begin trading on the Nasdaq Capital Market (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;) on a split-adjusted
basis at the opening of market on April 30, 2026.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">The Class A Ordinary Shares will continue to trade on the Nasdaq Capital
Market under the trading symbol &ldquo;UK&rdquo; but will trade under the following new CUSIP number: G9449A142. The Reverse Share Split
will reduce the number of outstanding ordinary shares of the Company from 6,779,498, including 6,660,111Class A ordinary shares and 119,387
Class B ordinary shares, to approximately 677,951 ordinary shares, including approximately 666,012 Class A ordinary shares and 11,939
Class B ordinary shares. Every ten (10) outstanding ordinary shares will be combined into and automatically become one post-Reverse Share
Split ordinary share. No fractional shares will be issued in connection with the Reverse Share Split. Instead, the Company will issue
one full post-Reverse Share Split share to any shareholder at a participant level who would have been entitled to receive a fractional
share as a result of the process.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center"></P>

